 "_note": "D74 (2026-10-27): WHEN JARVIS MUST ASK INSTEAD OF ACTING. Plain rules, no model: jarvis/plugins/_shared/ambiguity.py reads this file and runs before any plan or action in do_goal, quick_command and run_pc_task. A request that matches is turned into ONE short question (a jarvis_ask form: the candidates JARVIS can really find as buttons, plus 'Something else'), and when the owner answers, the ORIGINAL goal goes on with his answer put in. A request that names what it acts on ('open notepad', 'delete test.txt in Downloads') never matches. Kinds: either_or ('notepad or wordpad'), destructive (a delete with no named object), close (a 'close the window' that names no app), reference ('it', 'that file', 'the file from yesterday', 'the usual' with nothing in the request or the last task that settles it), slot (a required part is missing: to whom, which folder, what about, when, what to play, what name). Words are lists, so more can be added here without code: English, Telugu and Hindi in English letters (and a few in their own letters). A word list that is wrong asks too often (annoying) or too rarely (it guesses): tests/ambiguity_cases.json holds the labelled requests (clear ones must pass untouched, vague ones must ask). This file decides what JARVIS dares to guess, so it is console-only to change (policy SAFETY_COMPONENTS, push_gate PROTECTED); a missing or broken file falls back to a small built-in floor in ambiguity.py, never to 'guess everything'.",
